{"diagnosis": "Loopback read via reg_dat_do returned 0x25 instead of expected 0xa5 (TRAP: uart data mismatch got 0x25 want 0xa5). 0xa5 is 8'b10100101 whose low 7 bits are 7'b0100101 = 0x25, indicating 1-bit truncation of MSB. Root cause is line 42 declaring recv_buf_data as [7:1] (7 bits) instead of [7:0], so 8-bit recv_pattern assignment drops bit7 and reg_dat_do reports the truncated value.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@
 	reg [3:0] recv_state;
 	reg [31:0] recv_divcnt;
 	reg [7:0] recv_pattern;
-	reg [7:1] recv_buf_data;
+	reg [7:0] recv_buf_data;
 	reg recv_buf_valid;

 	reg [9:0] send_pattern;", "expected": "tohost PASS (no TRAP), uart loopback got 0xa5 want 0xa5"}

